# ============================================================================
# Notes:
# ============================================================================
# - All HIGH, MEDIUM, and LOW severity alerts are in base Debian packages, not application code
# - These packages are dependencies of the Python base image
# - Fixes require upstream Debian/Python base image updates
# - Container security best practices are followed:
#   * Run as non-root user (UID 1000)
#   * Minimal slim image with only required packages
#   * Regular base image updates via `apt-get upgrade`
#   * No system daemons running (Python is PID 1)
#   * Python abstractions isolate from C library vulnerabilities
# - Monitor Debian security tracker for updates
# - Re-evaluate suppressions when base image is updated
# - Many LOW severity CVEs are legacy/theoretical or affect unused tools/features
